<Project Sdk="AsmFoundation.Sdk/ASMSDK_VERSION">
  <!--
    AsmStatic.1: a static library written in assembly, for other assembly projects to link.
    "dotnet build" builds it for this machine under bin/<Configuration>/freestanding/<rid>/
    (AsmStatic.1.lib on Windows, libAsmStatic.1.a elsewhere). mul.asm is the x64 code (NASM),
    mul.s the ARM64 code (GNU syntax).

    An assembly project (a library or a program) uses it through one line in its .asmproj:
      <ProjectReference Include="../AsmStatic.1/AsmStatic.1.asmproj" />
    which links this library into it and puts include/ on its include path, so a NASM source
    there can %include "AsmStatic.1.inc" and call mul_ints. "dotnet pack" packs the library and
    include/ for every platform it lists, as a package other projects reference instead.

    The functions are HIDDEN_FUNCTION: callable by the code that links this library, but
    exported by none of the images it ends up in. FUNCTION would export them from each.

    Ship it for more platforms by listing them here:
      <RuntimeIdentifiers>win-x64;win-arm64;linux-x64;linux-arm64;osx-x64;osx-arm64</RuntimeIdentifiers>

    The SDK version is the one on the first line; change it there to upgrade.
    Documentation: https://asmfoundation.github.io/AsmSdk/guide/references-and-packages.html
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>StaticLibrary</OutputType>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
